# `yo fix <path> --migrate rc-clone` (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md decision 17,
# V2c) spells every implicit copy of a counted handle whose source stays
# alive: `Rc.clone(h)` / `Arc.clone(h)` for a handle (a local read again, a
# `&Rc(T)` parameter or a field returned, a by-value argument), `.clone()` for
# a `Clone` value holding one (`Node`, `Option(Rc(i32))`), `k : Rc.clone(k)`
# for a capture list's shorthand entry, and a capture list for a closure that
# captures a handle implicitly (not for one lent to `RefCell.with`, which
# borrows its captures), and `&` before a `match` scrutinee that is a field
# holding a handle (`match(&h.slot, ...)`), `&mut` when an arm writes through
# a binding (`fill`), and a clone of a module-level scrutinee or one an arm
# writes (`last_of`, `refresh`). A copy in a loop whose next iteration reads
# the source is cloned (`walk`); a `match` on a `&` parameter is left alone
# (`hits`). A last use (`moved := last`) is a move and is left alone; `Bare`
# holds a handle and is not `Clone`, so its copy is listed.
# The expected_tree pins the rewritten main.yo.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=240
